attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 25, `ppiA` to `tuf`, are carried by 96 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 3% of calls {S1}. The model names 54 to 100% of them, fewest at column 19, `tusD`, 54% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column breaks the spine**: column 26, `chiA`, shell, carried by 67%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2.c26, P}. Then columns 29 to 42, `gspO` to `gspB`, variable, carried by 65 to 72%, are [[type II secretion, pseudopilin]] {S4.c29-42, Q}. The last spine, columns 43 to 79, `rpsJ` to `dprA`, is [[ribosomal proteins]] {S5, Q}.

@model **The model names about as many genes on the spine columns as on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 96%, and hesitates less there, 0.05 against 0.18 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 26, `chiA`, is a variable column, at 0.48 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on persistent families.** Columns 43 to 79, `rpsJ` to `dprA`, are carried by 90 to 97% of chromosomes {S5}. The last column is `dprA`, in 90% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 98% of genes**, 0.07 bits on average, perplexity 1.1 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.24 against 0.05 bits, and names about as many genes, 96% against 98% {C}.

